        "updated_assessment": "The security dimension has escalated to its highest point in this monitoring cycle. The May 20 Vilnius drone alert — which drove the first civilian mass shelter alarm in an EU/NATO capital since Russia's 2022 invasion, sent the PM and President underground, closed Vilnius airport, and scrambled NATO jets — represents a qualitative threshold crossed: Lithuania's population and leadership are now operationally engaged in the drone warfare environment, not merely anticipating it. PM Ruginienė subsequently acknowledged systemic shelter access failures before the Seimas and ordered 24-hour shelter availability — confirming a concrete civil defense capability gap. Defense Minister Kaunas declared this the 'new reality' and said further incidents are 'highly probable.' The trilateral Baltic presidential joint statement on May 21 — calling for NATO to transition from air policing to a full air defense mission with counter-drone capabilities — is the most formal collective Alliance demand for regional air defense upgrading in this monitoring period, formalizing what was previously a bilateral presidential ask (Nausėda-Stubb). The police/border guard corruption scandal in the balloon smuggling network adds a structural new dimension: it reveals that the Belarusian balloon hybrid campaign has penetrated Lithuanian state security institutions, with officers facilitating rather than interdicting the smuggling. Domain 2 STRUC-02's characterization of the balloon campaign as state-sponsored remains supported, but the internal corruption dimension means the threat operates through Lithuanian institutions, not only against them — a materially more complex threat picture than last week's assessment captured.",
